body:
Test name says "long-press triggers context menu" but the test doesn't actually perform a long-press gesture or verify that a context menu appears. It only counts buttons and checks count >= 0, which is a trivial assertion. Consider either implementing actual long-press testing (e.g., using touchscreen with a delayed tap or manual touch events) and verifying context menu appearance, or removing/renaming this test to reflect its actual purpose.
```suggestion
  test('mobile viewport renders interactive buttons', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto(`${CONSOLE_BASE}/`, { waitUntil: 'networkidle' });
    await waitForReactMount(page);

    // Verify interactive elements are present and touchable
    const buttons = page.locator('button');
    const count = await buttons.count();
    expect(count).toBeGreaterThan(0);
```
